{
  "version": "outlines-v1",
  "about": "One outline row per kind of text, read by the one planner (src/english/outline-planner.ts; words composer, units 3 and 6; the Story lead's brief, Nov 24, 2026). A row names its sections in order; each section offers shapes, and a shape is an order of moves, each worded from data/english/parts/outline.json. A move ending in '?' may be left out. A section's `when` facts must hold for it to be said; `joins` keeps it in the paragraph before; `camera` is where the picture is while it is said. Shapes are picked by the speaker's recorded traits (`pull`) among those whose `needs` hold; no shape is forced on every point (owner, Nov 23: 'this is all following the same grammatical pattern'). An address's `occasion` section says what the day is: the inaugural's oath or the election that hired the speaker, a yearly address's report of the state of the union or the state (the move `report`, whose pieces each kind's writer gates on the facts the plan holds: its kind of address, the year's story, the mood). The rows hold no sentence.",
